From 9956b19fbd2a74b2ade280389300fa42be90c4d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:27:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] UPSTREAM:PROTOCOL:sigma_dut: Don't force PMF for WPA3 program

cmd_ap_set_wireless() forces dut->ap_pmf on every ap_set_wireless
call when dut->program is EHT or WPA3. For WPA3-FT tests, this
clobbers an explicit PMF,Required already set via ap_set_security
whenever a later ap_set_wireless call (e.g. FT_OA,Enable) arrives,
downgrading ieee80211w=2 to 1 and failing RSNCap_MFPR checks.

Drop the WPA3 case; EHT-only matches the pre-existing behavior this
override was meant for. EPPKE key management already derives its own
ieee80211w independent of dut->ap_pmf, so it is unaffected.

Signed-off-by: Priyadharshini Gowthaman <pgowtham@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 ap.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ap.c b/ap.c
index 85aaacb..cf84a59 100644
--- a/ap.c
+++ b/ap.c
@@ -1491,7 +1491,7 @@ static enum sigma_cmd_result cmd_ap_set_wireless(struct sigma_dut *dut,
 	    (dut->ap_interface_6g && dut->ap_interface_2g))
 		dut->ap_is_dual = 1;
 
-	if (dut->program == PROGRAM_EHT || dut->program == PROGRAM_WPA3) {
+	if (dut->program == PROGRAM_EHT) {
 		dut->ap_pmf = AP_PMF_OPTIONAL;
 		dut->ap_beacon_prot = 1;
 		if ((dut->ap_interface_5g || dut->ap_interface_2g) &&
-- 
2.34.1

